HookLabelPrefix = \"post-restore-node-cleanup.step.hook.operation.cattle.io/\""," ","-\t// RestartClusterStepHookLabelPrefix gates the final restart pass, after node cleanup. This","-\t// removes the temporary server-URL override and lets each node return to its normal","-\t// reconciliation.","+\t// RestartClusterStepHookLabelPrefix gates the final restart pass, after node cleanup. This removes the temporary","+\t// server-URL override and lets each node return to its normal reconciliation."," \tRestartClusterStepHookLabelPrefix = \"restart-cluster.step.hook.operation.cattle.io/\""," ","+\t// preflightInstructionName is the name of the Preflight step's instruction, and therefore the key its output is","+\t// saved under on the machine-plan secret.","+\tpreflightInstructionName = \"preflight\"","+","+\t// TokenHashCommandFormat is the shell command the Preflight step runs on every etcd node to hash the server token","+\t// persisted on disk, so it can be compared against the hash the distro stamped on the snapshot.","+\t// The single format argument is the distro data directory, where the token file is persisted.","+\t//","+\t// It has to reproduce in a shell what the distro's do which respects colons as part of the password, treating","+\t// everything after \"server:\" as the password.","+\t//","+\t// So two anchored, non-greedy substitutions recover the password: the first drops the `K10<CA-hash>::` prefix, the","+\t// second drops the `server:` username. `[^:]*` cannot cross a colon, which is what makes them non-greedy; a greedy","+\t// `.*:` would strip through the *last* colon. This also respects passwords ending in a colon.","+\t//","+\t// Whitespace is only trimmed at the edges, matching the bytes.TrimSpace the distro applies when it","+\t// reads the same file; deleting all whitespace would corrupt a password that contains a space.","+\t//","+\t// The missing/empty guards are not incidental. Every element of the derivation is a pipeline, so without them a",